 "problems": [
  "This table's column layout does not match the expected Schedule A schema (unit/type/floor/rooms/beds/baths/int_sf/sf2/ext_sf/price/pct/pct2/cc_m/cc_a/tax_m/tax_a/tax2_m/carry_m). There is no \"floor\" or \"rooms\" column. Beds/baths are combined codes like \"0 BR/1 BA\" or \"2 BR/2.5 BA\" - I left beds/baths blank and put the full code in note (int_sf column instead, per instructions for unclear codes, but here it is clear combined BR/BA; I used it as the \"note\"-like descriptor in place of proper beds/baths columns since no separate beds and baths columns exist). No separate int_sf column exists - \"Approximate Square Footage of Unit\" was used as int_sf. Terrace and Garden space are two separate outdoor area columns; since ext_sf rule requires one number and multiple areas go to note, I instead placed terrace in one slot and garden in another (nonstandard) - see individual rows where terrace/garden values appear in sf2/ext_sf positions inconsistently; this does not cleanly fit the schema. No cc_a column present - \"Annual Landscaping and Garden Charges\" placed in cc_a slot, which may be mislabeled. No tax2_m or carry_m distinctly separable from displayed \"Total Monthly Carrying Charges\" (used as carry_m). Commercial Totals row and Grand Totals row also printed on page 89 but not transcribed in TOTAL line (only Residential Totals used) - Commercial Totals: sf 2,630, pct 1.8188%, cc_m 1856, tax_m 5735, price not stated separately. Grand Totals: price 408470000, pct 100.0000%, cc_m 238858, tax_m 313681, int_sf 141879, ext_sf (terrace) 10899, garden 3615. Unit 1A is missing an offering price in the source text (shows blank/$ -). Floor numbers are embedded in unit numbers (e.g. \"1A\" = floor 1) but not given as separate column, so floor was left as \"-\"."
 ],
